39:     Input structure
40:     - The canvas background is black.
41:     - The only foreground object is one 4-connected five-pixel red plus.
42:     - The plus supplies a center, four diagonal gaps, and four cardinal arms.
43: 
44:     Rule
45:     - Preserve the red plus.
46:     - From each diagonal neighbor of the plus center, paint a blue ray to the grid edge.
47:     - From each cardinal arm, continue outward to the grid edge with the repeating color pattern teal, teal, yellow.
48: 
49:     Key insight
50:     - The red plus is a compact ray emitter: its diagonal gaps start the uniform blue diagonals, while each arm starts the same three-cell cardinal stripe pattern.
51:     """
52:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
