35: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
36:     """
37:     Paint one cell from each marker toward its nearer colored edge bar.
38: 
39:     Input structure
40:     - The background is the dominant color.
41:     - Two complete, opposite edge bars appear as either full rows or full columns.
42:     - The remaining foreground color marks isolated control pixels between the bars.
43: 
44:     Rule
45:     - For each control pixel, compare its distance to the two edge bars along the bar-to-bar axis.
46:     - Paint the adjacent background cell one step toward the nearer bar.
47:     - Use the nearer bar's color for that new cell and leave all existing pixels unchanged.
48: 
49:     Key insight
